      "seed": 440871677,
      "version": 156,
      "versionNonce": 507960995,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790067719209,
      "created": 1790010857340,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "I'm a bit worried about the crawling because we use standard Python\nurllib. Because I asked Perplexity, I just told him the entire architecture\nthat we use this urllib. And you told me this is a very fast library for\nstatic pages but most of the modern dark web pages have JavaScript as\nwell. Even HTTPX is not good so you are suggesting Playwright but\nshould we even change it because Playwright adds a whole lot more\ncomplexity? Maybe we could just stick with urllib ? And maybe in future\nwe could add Playwright or HTTPX.  ",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "CQ8_vcjRKOMQ9aSe17mLl",
      "originalText": "I'm a bit worried about the crawling because we use standard Python urllib. Because I asked Perplexity, I just told him the entire architecture that we use this urllib. And you told me this is a very fast library for static pages but most of the modern dark web pages have JavaScript as well. Even HTTPX is not good so you are suggesting Playwright but should we even change it because Playwright adds a whole lot more complexity? Maybe we could just stick with urllib ? And maybe in future we could add Playwright or HTTPX.  ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
