      "updated": 1790067719210,
      "created": 1790066366084,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "6. OPENCODE ISOLATED WORKSPACE & AI AGENT (Host)\n• Now again, all the things that happened like the logsmith, the telemetry, and the offset profiler, all that\ninformation and all their output was stored in the database, in the tables, as well as in the folder which you\ncreated in step 1.\nThat folder will now contain the opencode metadata from the crawling step: all the crawled information, like\nwhat all pages were crawled, their raw text, outbound links, raw HTML, all that thing, and HTML/.html files\nas well, separately. It is better for opencode to understand the output of the logsmith agent, the logsmith\nphase, the stylometric phase, and the offset profiler phase, all that output in a single folder. For opencode, for\nthat specific job, it will be properly structured and stored.\nAgain after the stylometric and oxy profiler phase, we come to opencode or the AI phase. Since we have now\ncollected all the information, all the context for AI, we will give AI the prompt: \"You are an NTRO AI agent\nspecializing in XYZ and you have to read all the files in this folder for this job.\" That folder will also contain\nthe original query, fanout query, and all the information that ever happened for that specific job.\nopencode gets the entire context and he will also draft a prompt, create a prompt, which will be good for it\nand explain to him each and everything from that folder:\n- What files are there?\n- What each file would mean\n- What the HTML files would mean\n- What the stylometric folder would have\n- What its output would mean\nopencode has a great idea about everything and then\n\nAnd then we would tell him to read through every single thing and create a graph. There will be two types\nof graph:\n1. A Cytoscape graph. I don't know how that is made.\n2. A Mermaid.js graph.\nYou could only keep the Cytoscape graph if you want but I am telling you about the Mermaid graph because\nwe could make it look a bit better. opencode has to read through all the HTML files and everything else and\nthen make a graph connecting everything that had been done in that job.\n\nI made an example cytoscape.js graph so you may take a look at it. :\n\nimport cytoscape from \"cytoscape\";\n\nconst cy = cytoscape({\n  container: document.getElementById(\"threat-graph\"),\n\n  elements: [\n    // Nodes\n    { data: { id: \"orgA\", label: \"Organization A\", type: \"organization\", ring: 3 } },\n\n    { data: { id: \"orgB\", label: \"Organization B\", type: \"organization\", ring: 2 } },\n    { data: { id: \"alias\", label: \"Person / Alias\", type: \"person\", ring: 2 } },\n    { data: { id: \"guns\", label: \"Firearms\", type: \"product\", ring: 2 } },\n    { data: { id: \"drugs\", label: \"Drugs\", type: \"product\", ring: 2 } },\n    { data: { id: \"market\", label: \"Marketplace\", type: \"website\", ring: 2 } },\n    { data: { id: \"wallet\", label: \"Crypto Wallet\", type: \"wallet\", ring: 2 } },\n\n    { data: { id: \"domain\", label: \"Domain\", type: \"website\", ring: 1 } },\n    { data: { id: \"evidence\", label: \"Source Evidence\", type: \"evidence\", ring: 1 } },\n    { data: { id: \"lead\", label: \"Investigation Lead\", type: \"lead\", ring: 1 } },\n\n    // Directed relationships\n    { data: { id: \"e1\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"orgB\", label: \"CONNECTED TO\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e2\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"alias\", label: \"CONNECTED TO\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e3\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"guns\", label: \"SELLS\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e4\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"drugs\", label: \"SELLS\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e5\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"market\", label: \"USES\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e6\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"wallet\", label: \"USES\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e7\", source: \"market\", target: \"domain\", label: \"HOSTED ON\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e8\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"evidence\", label: \"SUPPORTED BY\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e9\", source: \"evidence\", target: \"lead\", label: \"GENERATES LEAD\" } }\n  ],\n\n  style: [\n    {\n      selector: \"node\",\n      style: {\n        \"label\": \"data(label)\",\n        \"text-wrap\": \"wrap\",\n        \"text-max-width\": \"100px\",\n        \"text-valign\": \"center\",\n        \"text-halign\": \"center\",\n        \"color\": \"#ffffff\",\n        \"font-size\": \"11px\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#374151\",\n        \"border-width\": 2,\n        \"border-color\": \"#9ca3af\",\n        \"width\": \"65px\",\n        \"height\": \"65px\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Organization: circle\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"organization\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"ellipse\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#991b1b\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#ef4444\",\n        \"width\": \"95px\",\n        \"height\": \"95px\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Person / Alias: circle\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"person\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"ellipse\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#1d4ed8\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#60a5fa\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Products: rounded rectangles\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"product\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"roundrectangle\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#166534\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#4ade80\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Websites: rectangle\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"website\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"rectangle\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#4c1d95\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#a78bfa\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Wallet: cylinder\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"wallet\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"barrel\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#92400e\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#fbbf24\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Evidence: document-like shape\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"evidence\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"rectangle\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#374151\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#d1d5db\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Investigation lead: diamond\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"lead\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"diamond\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#854d0e\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#facc15\",\n        \"width\": \"85px\",\n        \"height\": \"85px\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // All edges\n    {\n      selector: \"edge\",\n      style: {\n        \"curve-style\": \"bezier\",\n        \"width\": 2,\n        \"line-color\": \"#9ca3af\",\n        \"target-arrow-color\": \"#d1d5db\",\n        \"target-arrow-shape\": \"triangle\",\n        \"label\": \"data(label)\",\n        \"font-size\": \"8px\",\n        \"color\": \"#d1d5db\",\n        \"text-background-color\": \"#111827\",\n        \"text-background-opacity\": 0.9,\n        \"text-background-padding\": \"3px\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Highlight selected node\n    {\n      selector: \"node:selected\",\n      style: {\n        \"border-color\": \"#facc15\",\n        \"border-width\": 4\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n\n  layout: {\n    name: \"concentric\",\n    fit: true,\n    padding: 60,\n    avoidOverlap: true,\n    spacingFactor: 1.4,\n    minNodeSpacing: 40,\n\n    // Higher values go closer to the center\n    concentric: node => node.data(\"ring\"),\n\n    levelWidth: () => 1,\n\n    startAngle: 0,\n    clockwise: true,\n    animate: true\n  }\n});\n ",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "6. OPENCODE ISOLATED WORKSPACE & AI AGENT (Host)\n• Now again, all the things that happened like the logsmith, the telemetry, and the offset profiler, all that information and all their output was stored in the database, in the tables, as well as in the folder which you created in step 1.\nThat folder will now contain the opencode metadata from the crawling step: all the crawled information, like what all pages were crawled, their raw text, outbound links, raw HTML, all that thing, and HTML/.html files as well, separately. It is better for opencode to understand the output of the logsmith agent, the logsmith phase, the stylometric phase, and the offset profiler phase, all that output in a single folder. For opencode, for that specific job, it will be properly structured and stored.\nAgain after the stylometric and oxy profiler phase, we come to opencode or the AI phase. Since we have now collected all the information, all the context for AI, we will give AI the prompt: \"You are an NTRO AI agent specializing in XYZ and you have to read all the files in this folder for this job.\" That folder will also contain the original query, fanout query, and all the information that ever happened for that specific job.\nopencode gets the entire context and he will also draft a prompt, create a prompt, which will be good for it and explain to him each and everything from that folder:\n- What files are there?\n- What each file would mean\n- What the HTML files would mean\n- What the stylometric folder would have\n- What its output would mean\nopencode has a great idea about everything and then\n\nAnd then we would tell him to read through every single thing and create a graph. There will be two types of graph:\n1. A Cytoscape graph. I don't know how that is made.\n2. A Mermaid.js graph.\nYou could only keep the Cytoscape graph if you want but I am telling you about the Mermaid graph because we could make it look a bit better. opencode has to read through all the HTML files and everything else and then make a graph connecting everything that had been done in that job.\n\nI made an example cytoscape.js graph so you may take a look at it. :\n\nimport cytoscape from \"cytoscape\";\n\nconst cy = cytoscape({\n  container: document.getElementById(\"threat-graph\"),\n\n  elements: [\n    // Nodes\n    { data: { id: \"orgA\", label: \"Organization A\", type: \"organization\", ring: 3 } },\n\n    { data: { id: \"orgB\", label: \"Organization B\", type: \"organization\", ring: 2 } },\n    { data: { id: \"alias\", label: \"Person / Alias\", type: \"person\", ring: 2 } },\n    { data: { id: \"guns\", label: \"Firearms\", type: \"product\", ring: 2 } },\n    { data: { id: \"drugs\", label: \"Drugs\", type: \"product\", ring: 2 } },\n    { data: { id: \"market\", label: \"Marketplace\", type: \"website\", ring: 2 } },\n    { data: { id: \"wallet\", label: \"Crypto Wallet\", type: \"wallet\", ring: 2 } },\n\n    { data: { id: \"domain\", label: \"Domain\", type: \"website\", ring: 1 } },\n    { data: { id: \"evidence\", label: \"Source Evidence\", type: \"evidence\", ring: 1 } },\n    { data: { id: \"lead\", label: \"Investigation Lead\", type: \"lead\", ring: 1 } },\n\n    // Directed relationships\n    { data: { id: \"e1\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"orgB\", label: \"CONNECTED TO\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e2\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"alias\", label: \"CONNECTED TO\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e3\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"guns\", label: \"SELLS\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e4\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"drugs\", label: \"SELLS\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e5\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"market\", label: \"USES\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e6\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"wallet\", label: \"USES\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e7\", source: \"market\", target: \"domain\", label: \"HOSTED ON\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e8\", source: \"orgA\", target: \"evidence\", label: \"SUPPORTED BY\" } },\n    { data: { id: \"e9\", source: \"evidence\", target: \"lead\", label: \"GENERATES LEAD\" } }\n  ],\n\n  style: [\n    {\n      selector: \"node\",\n      style: {\n        \"label\": \"data(label)\",\n        \"text-wrap\": \"wrap\",\n        \"text-max-width\": \"100px\",\n        \"text-valign\": \"center\",\n        \"text-halign\": \"center\",\n        \"color\": \"#ffffff\",\n        \"font-size\": \"11px\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#374151\",\n        \"border-width\": 2,\n        \"border-color\": \"#9ca3af\",\n        \"width\": \"65px\",\n        \"height\": \"65px\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Organization: circle\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"organization\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"ellipse\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#991b1b\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#ef4444\",\n        \"width\": \"95px\",\n        \"height\": \"95px\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Person / Alias: circle\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"person\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"ellipse\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#1d4ed8\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#60a5fa\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Products: rounded rectangles\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"product\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"roundrectangle\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#166534\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#4ade80\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Websites: rectangle\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"website\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"rectangle\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#4c1d95\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#a78bfa\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Wallet: cylinder\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"wallet\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"barrel\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#92400e\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#fbbf24\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Evidence: document-like shape\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"evidence\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"rectangle\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#374151\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#d1d5db\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Investigation lead: diamond\n    {\n      selector: 'node[type=\"lead\"]',\n      style: {\n        \"shape\": \"diamond\",\n        \"background-color\": \"#854d0e\",\n        \"border-color\": \"#facc15\",\n        \"width\": \"85px\",\n        \"height\": \"85px\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // All edges\n    {\n      selector: \"edge\",\n      style: {\n        \"curve-style\": \"bezier\",\n        \"width\": 2,\n        \"line-color\": \"#9ca3af\",\n        \"target-arrow-color\": \"#d1d5db\",\n        \"target-arrow-shape\": \"triangle\",\n        \"label\": \"data(label)\",\n        \"font-size\": \"8px\",\n        \"color\": \"#d1d5db\",\n        \"text-background-color\": \"#111827\",\n        \"text-background-opacity\": 0.9,\n        \"text-background-padding\": \"3px\"\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Highlight selected node\n    {\n      selector: \"node:selected\",\n      style: {\n        \"border-color\": \"#facc15\",\n        \"border-width\": 4\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n\n  layout: {\n    name: \"concentric\",\n    fit: true,\n    padding: 60,\n    avoidOverlap: true,\n    spacingFactor: 1.4,\n    minNodeSpacing: 40,\n\n    // Higher values go closer to the center\n    concentric: node => node.data(\"ring\"),\n\n    levelWidth: () => 1,\n\n    startAngle: 0,\n    clockwise: true,\n    animate: true\n  }\n});\n ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
